      "heading": "Side Effects, Precautions, and Warnings for Blood Sugar",
      "body": "<p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.1rem;\">Side effects, precautions, and warnings for blood sugar management with Metabosana are important considerations for anyone looking to incorporate this supplement into their diabetes care routine. The formulation contains a blend of well‑studied natural compounds—alpha‑lipoic acid, green tea EGCG, berberine HCl, chromium picolinate, banaba leaf, zinc gluconate, milk thistle, resveratrol, Korean ginseng, and cayenne. Each of these ingredients has been investigated for their influence on glucose metabolism, insulin sensitivity, and oxidative stress, but they can also produce mild adverse effects when taken in excess or in combination with other medications.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.1rem;\">Common side effects reported with the individual ingredients include mild gastrointestinal upset, diarrhea, and, rarely, nausea For example, berberine can stimulate intestinal motility, while green tea catechins may irritate the stomach lining in sensitive individuals Because the doses in Metabosana are lower than those used in many clinical trials, the risk of adverse events is modest</p>\n<p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.1rem;\">Nonetheless, users should monitor for any digestive discomfort and adjust the dose if necessary In most cases, the supplement is well tolerated, but individuals with a history of gastrointestinal disorders should start with a lower dose and observe tolerance.</p>\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;color:#064e3b;font-size:.95rem;margin:1.75rem 0 .75rem;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px dashed #d1d5db;\">Drug Interaction Table: Potential Interaction Risks</p>\n<div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"md-table\" style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;border-spacing:0;background:#fff;font-size:.9rem;table-layout:fixed;\"><thead><tr><th class=\"tbl-th\" style=\"background:#064e3b;color:#fff;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:.75rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;padding:.875rem 1.0625rem;text-align:left;border-right:2px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18);border-bottom:3px solid #059669;\">Medication</th><th class=\"tbl-th\" style=\"background:#064e3b;color:#fff;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:.75rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;padding:.875rem 1.0625rem;text-align:left;border-right:2px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18);border-bottom:3px solid #059669;\">Interaction Type</th><th class=\"tbl-th\" style=\"background:#064e3b;color:#fff;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:.75rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;padding:.875rem 1.0625rem;text-align:left;border-right:2px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18);border-bottom:3px solid #059669;\">Recommendation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=\"tbl-row-even\" style=\"background:#f0fdf4;\"><td class=\"tbl-td\" style=\"padding:.8125rem 1.0625rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;color:#374151;border-right:1.5px solid #d1fae5;border-bottom:1.5px solid #d1fae5;\">Insulin</td><td class=\"tbl-td\" style=\"padding:.8125rem 1.0625rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;color:#374151;border-right:1.5px solid #d1fae5;border-bottom:1.5px solid #d1fae5;\">May increase hypoglycaemia risk</td><td class=\"tbl-td\" style=\"padding:.8125rem 1.0625rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;color:#374151;border-right:1.5px solid #d1fae5;border-bottom:1.5px solid #d1fae5;\">Consult your prescribing doctor before combining</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-odd\" style=\"background:#fff;\"><td class=\"tbl-td\" style=\"padding:.8125rem 1.0625rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;color:#374151;border-right:1.5px solid #d1fae5;border-bottom:1.5px solid #d1fae5;\">Metformin</td><td class=\"tbl-td\" style=\"padding:.8125rem 1.0625rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;color:#374151;border-right:1.5px solid #d1fae5;border-bottom:1.5px solid #d1fae5;\">Possible additive GI effects</td><td class=\"tbl-td\" style=\"padding:.8125rem 1.0625rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;color:#374151;border-right:1.5px solid #d1fae5;border-bottom:1.5px solid #d1fae5;\">Monitor tolerance adjust dose if needed</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-even\" style=\"background:#f0fdf4;\"><td class=\"tbl-td\" style=\"padding:.8125rem 1.0625rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;color:#374151;border-right:1.5px solid #d1fae5;border-bottom:1.5px solid #d1fae5;\">ACE inhibitors</td><td class=\"tbl-td\" style=\"padding:.8125rem 1.0625rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;color:#374151;border-right:1.5px solid #d1fae5;border-bottom:1.5px solid #d1fae5;\">No significant interaction</td><td class=\"tbl-td\" style=\"padding:.8125rem 1.0625rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;color:#374151;border-right:1.5px solid #d1fae5;border-bottom:1.5px solid #d1fae5;\">Continue as prescribed</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-odd\" style=\"background:#fff;\"><td class=\"tbl-td\" style=\"padding:.8125rem 1.0625rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;color:#374151;border-right:1.5px solid #d1fae5;border-bottom:1.5px solid #d1fae5;\">Statins</td><td class=\"tbl-td\" style=\"padding:.8125rem 1.0625rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;color:#374151;border-right:1.5px solid #d1fae5;border-bottom:1.5px solid #d1fae5;\">Possible mild GI upset</td><td class=\"tbl-td\" style=\"padding:.8125rem 1.0625rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;color:#374151;border-right:1.5px solid #d1fae5;border-bottom:1.5px solid #d1fae5;\">Monitor liver enzymes if combined</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-even\" style=\"background:#f0fdf4;\"><td class=\"tbl-td\" style=\"padding:.8125rem 1.0625rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;color:#374151;border-right:1.5px solid #d1fae5;border-bottom:1.5px solid #d1fae5;\">Anticoagulants</td><td class=\"tbl-td\" style=\"padding:.8125rem 1.0625rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;color:#374151;border-right:1.5px solid #d1fae5;border-bottom:1.5px solid #d1fae5;\">No known interaction</td><td class=\"tbl-td\" style=\"padding:.8125rem 1.0625rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;color:#374151;border-right:1.5px solid #d1fae5;border-bottom:1.5px solid #d1fae5;\">Maintain regular monitoring</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"tbl-source\" style=\"font-size:.8rem;color:#6b7280;font-style:italic;margin:.6rem 0 1.75rem;padding-left:.2rem;border-top:1px dashed #e5e7eb;padding-top:.6rem;\">(Baicus et al., 2024)</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout-warning\" style=\"border-radius:.625rem;padding:1.1rem 1.4rem;margin:1.25rem 0;font-size:.9375rem;line-height:1.7;background:#fff7ed;border-left:5px solid #f97316;color:#7c2d12;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 .75rem;\"><strong>Warning:</strong> People with kidney or liver impairment should discuss use with a healthcare professional, as some ingredients may accumulate in reduced organ function.</p><p style=\"margin:0;\">For instance, milk thistle and resveratrol are metabolized by the liver, and chronic use could potentially affect hepatic enzyme activity. Similarly, berberine is excreted renally, and impaired kidney function may increase systemic exposure.</p></div>\n<p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.1rem;\">Action tip: Review all current medications with your doctor before starting. This includes over‑the‑counter supplements, herbal remedies, and prescription drugs. The combination of Metabosana with insulin or other glucose‑lowering agents can potentiate hypoglycaemia; therefore, blood glucose should be monitored closely during the first few weeks of use. If you experience persistent nausea, diarrhea, or any other adverse symptom, discontinue the supplement and seek medical advice.</p>\n",
      "actionTip": "Consult your healthcare provider before making changes to your routine.",
